  "body": "The **content models** part of the [head of the section of the spec for the `option` element](url) says;\n\n> If the element has no label attribute: Text that is not inter-element whitespace.\n\nThat means an empty `option` (one which doesn’t contain any text that is not inter-element whitespace) must have a `label` attribute.\n\nBut there are a number of existing examples in the spec that are non-conforming to that spec requirements, because they have empty `option` elements without `label` elements. At least one of those seems to date from as long back as the Web Forms 2.0 days, so I think it’s just likely that none of them got updated when the requirement above was first added.\n\nSo let’s update those examples to make them conform to the current spec requirements. \n",
